[
  {
    "description": "  Subject-scoped content rules (sovereign-ai-bots #98) let an operator scope a\n  rule to the message SUBJECT only: `--type content --contains <text> --scope\n  subject`. On the live classification path the rule must match `message.subject`\n  and nothing else — never the body.\n\n  sovereign-ai-bots #122 is the regression these scenarios guard: the subject\n  filter passed the unit/e2e stubs but was silently skipped on the real scan\n  loop, so a subject-scoped rule also matched the body and mis-classified\n  out-of-scope mail. PR#123 added unit coverage of the `scan` loop; this feature\n  closes the remaining gap by driving real email through the LIVE node (SMTP ->\n  Proton Bridge -> scan -> zone history / alerts) and asserting both halves:\n    - an IN-scope message (marker in the subject) IS escalated by the rule, and\n      the alert cites the subject filter as the reason; and\n    - an OUT-of-scope message (same-shaped marker in the BODY only, marker-free\n      subject) is NOT mis-classified — the subject rule stays inert.",
